# `/home` Cinematic Scroll Experience — Final Implementation Plan

---

## 0. Visual Truth Principle

> **The browser-rendered result is the final authority.**

All numerical values in this plan — percentages, scale multipliers, camera Z positions, FOV values, particle counts, timings, opacity values, easing durations — are **implementation starting points**, not final specifications.

The final values must be tuned from the actual Chrome-rendered result. For every major visual target, the acceptance criterion is defined visually:

| Target | Starting Value | Visual Acceptance Criterion |
|--------|---------------|---------------------------|
| Q_QUEST size | `clamp(4.5rem, 13vw, 10rem)` | Title anchors the opening scene, feels dominant and bold |
| Sphere at arrival hold | camera Z ≈ 3.3 | Sphere visually occupies ~75–80% of viewport height |
| Launch Pad initial reveal | `scale(2.5)` | Heading dominates ~70–75% of viewport width while remaining legible |
| Fragment count (desktop) | 35–55 primary + 10–25 secondary | Breakup reads as "transformation" not "particle effect" |
| Anticipation hold | progress 0.55–0.68 | Perceptible cinematic beat — viewer registers the sphere's importance |

If a starting value produces a poor visual result, it must be changed. The plan guides implementation; Chrome validates it.

